## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a streaming NLP system that handles multiple languages, domain adaptation, drift monitoring, latency budgets, and privacy considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual NER with adapters
- Drift monitoring and active learning
- Domain gazetteers and retrieval augmentation
- Privacy: data minimization and differential privacy
- Evaluation: streaming metrics, latency budgets, OOD checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-inference sketch with adapters
async function predict(text, model) {
  const tokens = tokenize(text);
  const enc = model.encode(tokens);
  const logits = await model.predict(enc);
  return decodeEntities(logits, tokens);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify and react to drift in production?
- How would you structure the entity schema with provenance and versioning?
- How would you audit and mitigate bias across languages?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a compact, privacy-preserving NLP module that runs entirely on-device, handles multilingual input, and delivers a concrete deliverable with measurable constraints.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference
- Language detection for EN/ES/FR
- Lightweight sentiment signals
- Sentence selection heuristics
- Rollout and evaluation plan

## Code Example

```javascript
function scoreSentence(sent, lang) {
  // simple placeholder: use length and keyword hits
  const keywords = {
    en: ["great","love","best"],
    es: ["genial","me encanta","mejor"],
    fr: ["super","aimé","meilleur"]
  }[lang] || [];
  let score = sent.length;
  for (const kw of keywords) {
    if (sent.toLowerCase().includes(kw)) score += 5;
  }
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What if reviews mix languages within a sentence? How would you robustly detect language?
- How would you handle mislabeling when sentiment is subtle?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design modular, scalable NLP systems that evolve without full retraining, while meeting strict latency and privacy constraints across multiple languages.

## Key Concepts
- Adapter-based fine-tuning
- Multilingual encoders
- Real-time latency requirements
- Privacy-preserving logging
- Canary rollout and drift detection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example of adding an adapter for a new intent using adapters
const tokenizer = loadTokenizer("xlm-roberta-base");
const model = loadModelWithHeads("xlm-roberta-base");
model.addAdapter("refund_policy_update");
model.trainAdapter("refund_policy_update");
// fine-tune with a few hundred examples
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate that new intents do not degrade existing ones?
- How would you handle multilingual data drift across EN/ES/PT?
